+// Vertex positions computed bit-identically by every shader that draws the same geometry, as on the
+// console (Xenia marks the position invariant for the same reason). Multipass renderers (UE3: a depth
+// pass, then a pass per light with an EQUAL depth test) otherwise lose pixels wherever two translated
+// shaders round the position differently: speckled, smeared surfaces. The position is `precise`, and
+// vertex shaders carrying the mark below compile with IEEE strictness (renderer.cpp), so neither fxc
+// nor the driver fuses or reorders that math per shader. REGPU_NO_PRECISE_POSITION=1: off (A/B; read
+// at translation, so the two forms cache apart).
+bool PrecisePosition()
+{
+    static const bool on = getenv("REGPU_NO_PRECISE_POSITION") == nullptr;
+    return on;
+}
